WHATNOW

What tam-hide is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise it
at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-27, with W12

STATE

  Version 0.3.0 on dev (W12). Phase P2a (workstation readiness) is complete
  and verified on host (no live host changes):
  - Live `passcodes.db` hot-reload (`RELOAD_STORE`, `tam-hidectl reload-store`,
    `SIGHUP`, `ExecReload` in `systemd/tam-hided.service`) preserves the
    existing store on corrupt/unreadable reloads and wipes pending `PICK`.
  - Automatic `seat0` session discovery and reconciliation
    (`src/session_sync.{h,c}`, `controller_reconcile_sessions()`) via
    `libsystemd` `sd-login` (`USE_SYSTEMD?=1`, `--no-logind`, and portable
    `USE_SYSTEMD=0` build), preserving `lock_confirmed` for unchanged
    `(vt, uid, kind)` entries and failing closed to `lock_vt` when the active
    user session ends.
  - Interactive non-disclosing console passcode and picker prompt on `lock_vt`
    (`src/vt_prompt.{h,c}`, `--no-vt-prompt`), tested end-to-end over a PTY
    (`tests/test_vt_prompt.c`).
  - `tam-hide` auto-discovers `/run/tam-hide/auth.sock` + `XDG_VTNR` with
    seamless PAM fallback when `tam-hided` is absent (`--pam-only` opt-out).
  - Verified with `make clean && make all test test-headless` (6 unit/PTY
    suites + 2-output headless `tam-pane` suite) and
    `make clean && make USE_SYSTEMD=0 all test`.

NEXT

  1. Phase P2b (`0.3.1`): Run disposable KVM/QEMU verification of `0.3.0` with
     `tam-pane` on DRM/KMS, `sd-login` automatic session discovery, `tty6`
     console prompt unlock/picker, and `SIGHUP` passcode reload (zero live host
     changes).
  2. Phase P2c (`0.3.2`): Live workstation rollout once Fred selects a target
     host and authorizes installation with a recorded rollback point.

WAITING FOR FRED

  Approval and target host selection before any live `tam-hided.service` or
  seat/login integration.

WATCH OUT

  Do not install `systemd/tam-hided.service` on a live host without Fred's
  explicit approval and a recorded rollback point.
  Keep `make install` installing `tam-hide` alone until live seat rollout is
  authorized (`make install-seat` is opt-in).
  Never add auth-bypass CLI flags to `build/tam-hide`.
